    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a volatile slate today, anchored by **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) and **Cole Carrigg** (71.23). **Jacob Wilson** benefits immensely from a plus-matchup against Valdez, leveraging a favorable park factor and a premium spot in the leadoff hole to maximize scoring potential. Similarly, **Cole Carrigg** is positioned for a high-output performance; his switch-hitting ability combined with a soft matchup against Avila\u2019s 4.92 xERA makes him a cornerstone of today's production. **Drake Baldwin** also vaults into the elite tier (70.88) by virtue of batting leadoff against the vulnerable Mikolas, providing us with a rare, high-efficiency anchor at the catcher position.\n\nWhile the top of the lineup is primed for success, the middle of the order faces significant headwinds. We are forcing **Gunnar Henderson** (50.48) and **Coby Mayo** (53.52) into the lineup despite an imposing matchup against Sanchez; the optimizer heavily penalizes their scores due to the pitcher\u2019s elite ability to suppress the running game, which directly threatens our priority category of stolen bases. On the bench, **Denzer Guzman** (44.21) remains our most difficult omission, narrowly missing the cut behind the superior efficiency projections of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Dominic Smith**. The decision ultimately tilted against **Denzer Guzman** due to his projected lower floor and disadvantageous spot in the lineup. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the risk profile of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**, as their high-end talent is being suppressed by a pitcher who excels at limiting the very category that defines our team strategy. Conversely, **Jackson Merrill** (69.10) represents a sturdy start against Mahle, maintaining strong efficiency despite minor park-factor headwinds. Monitor the status of **Andy Pages** (53.37), as his proximity to our 40-point \"below floor\" threshold suggests that any late lineup shifts pushing him down the order would necessitate an immediate re-evaluation. With **Jordan Westburg** confirmed on the IL, we have limited flexibility, making it imperative that our high-scoring anchors deliver early to maintain our competitive pace in the 5x5 standings.",
